# Environment presets for the multiplayer server endpoint (see src/net/connection.ts).

# --- DEV ---
# Local development: when VITE_SERVER_URL is unset (or empty) the client
# automatically connects to the local dev server, so `npm run dev` needs no
# environment at all. Setting it explicitly to the same value changes nothing:
VITE_SERVER_URL=ws://localhost:8787

# --- PROD (GitHub Pages) ---
# Production is configured by CI, not a local .env. The GitHub Pages workflow
# (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) bakes VITE_SERVER_URL into the build from a
# repository Variable:
#
#   Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > Variables
#   VITE_SERVER_URL = wss://your-server.example
#
# The workflow fails the build if that variable is missing, so a Pages deploy
# never ships a build wired to a localhost server. Set ALLOW_EMPTY_SERVER_URL
# to 'true' in the same place only to deploy deliberately without multiplayer.